source: tui/src/bottom_pane/security_level_picker_issue_443_tests.rs
expression: "render(&picker, 80)"
---
Switch to Aggressive?
These settings replace yours in Corbanu Terminal sessions and their child
agents:
"now" shows this session; web search, environment, shell and roles are as loaded
at launch.
• Sandbox now: commands can write to the current folder
  Aggressive: write only in the current folder (where the Corbanu home and the
    nested-launch registry stay read-only): no extra writable folders, no /tmp
    or $TMPDIR; approved commands stay inside it too; escalation and permission-
    request tools are off; the project's .git, .codex and .agents stay read-
    only, even with Grant once (it only lets one command write git hooks and
    config kept outside a .git folder and, when the current folder holds your
    home folder, start-up files, login agents and .claude settings); reading
    credential files (.env, .env.* and .envrc files, also ones created later;
    not .env.example, .env.sample or .env.template; SSH, cloud and CLI tokens)
    or Corbanu's sign-in, vault, config and history is denied to agent commands
    and is never granted, not even once (switch to Permissive in /security to
    allow it); on Linux and Windows a command is stopped when such a file
    appears while it runs, and a process already waiting for that file can read
    it in the moment before the stop; a credential file that is a link must be
    replaced with a regular file or moved out of the folder
• Approvals now: on-request (reviewer: you)
  Aggressive: untrusted: you approve every command that is not known read-only
    (reviewer: you, never auto-review)
• Network now: on for agent commands; web search live
  Aggressive: off for agent commands; web search off
• Vault now: the vault store and sign-in file are readable to agent commands
  Aggressive: the vault store and sign-in file are unreadable to agent commands,
    and direct `corbanu vault …` commands are refused; secret-like environment
    variables (KEY, SECRET, TOKEN, VAULT, PASSWORD, PASSPHRASE, CREDENTIAL) are
    removed, and with secretless_agent_launch on so is every other variable
    outside an allowlist (for example PATH, HOME, locale, terminal, proxy and
    tool locations; set others explicitly in shell_environment_policy.set);
    login profiles and shell snapshots are not used
• Model keys now: Corbanu reads provider keys itself (broker_model_auth off)
  Aggressive: provider API keys from the environment or the vault are held by
    the isolated credential broker, which sends model requests for Corbanu
    (sign-in tokens are passed to it; command, AWS and header sign-ins are not
    brokered; realtime and websockets are off); if it cannot start, model
    requests are refused, never sent directly (broker_model_auth;
    `broker_model_auth = false` in your own config keeps it off)
• Child agents now: spawned agents get this session's values
  Aggressive: spawned agents get the same values; custom roles that would change
    them are refused at start; Claude panes are refused because Claude Code runs
    outside the sandbox, unless contained_external_agents and
    secretless_agent_launch run them in it, asking you before every command,
    file edit and web request (reading files stays automatic) (Claude Code sign-
    in still runs)
• Nested agents: refuse. An agent command that starts another agent (`corbanu
    exec`, `review`, `resume`, `fork`, a new session, `app-server` or `mcp-
    server`) is refused.
Press n to switch between refuse and pass. Nested launches read this when they
start.
Preflight passed: no known raw-secret route stays open to agents or the model.
Controls ready: 6 of 6 (OS sandbox, Secretless agent launch, Isolated credential
broker, Secret output gate, Untrusted-content labels, Vault)
Conversations recorded before the restart cannot be resumed under Aggressive.
Limits: Only fixed locations are checked; secrets in other files, under innocent
names, are not found. Values are matched by name, by common key shapes and
against Corbanu's own secret variables; other encodings are missed. The vault
is not opened; whether its key unlocks it is checked when a credential is
used. Browser profiles and keychains are listed, not read. MCP servers, hooks
and notify commands run outside the sandbox; only their configured secrets are
checked.
Unchanged: model and provider, MCP servers, apps and hooks (they run outside the
sandbox), wallet scopes, and commands you have already allowed permanently (they
skip the prompt but stay sandboxed). `corbanu exec` that you start yourself
and IDE sessions are not covered yet, except that they also hold provider keys
in the credential broker and, while they run on this Corbanu home, take Core's
Aggressive protections and approval for every command.
The rows above take effect when you restart Corbanu Terminal (you can restart
right after saving); until then this window's session keeps its current
settings, apart from Core's level and approval for every command (below). Your
config.toml is not modified.
Core's level is saved as Aggressive as soon as you confirm: agent commands
cannot run `corbanu vault …` and cannot open protected paths (the vault
store, sign-in files, credential files in your home folder such as .ssh, .aws
and .netrc, and Corbanu's config, history and state), sensitive surfaces need
a grant, external content reaches the model labelled untrusted, and memory
summaries stop. This window's session has not started yet: when it starts
here, it takes Core's level and approval for every command, and so do the other
sessions you start here before you restart. The other sessions of this Corbanu
Terminal running on this Corbanu home take it as soon as you confirm, with
approval for every command from their next turn.
Other Corbanu Terminals running on this Corbanu home take Core's Aggressive
protections and approval for every command within about a second of confirming,
and each says so; the rest of Aggressive starts there when they restart.
n refuse/pass · enter confirm and save · esc back, nothing changes
